---
import {Button} from '../dmf-ui/button';
---
<section class="docs-section docs-prose" aria-labelledby="contrast-options"><h2 id="contrast-options">Brand exceptions and existing alternatives</h2><p>CB and HUI filled primary actions retain white labels by explicit owner preference, on unchanged brand fills. The base pairs measure approximately 2.57:1 and 4.29:1 for normal text; hover opacity can reduce contrast further. These exceptions are not WCAG AA acceptance.</p><p>When normal-size text must meet 4.5:1, use the existing outline action on an appropriate surface and test the actual state. This changes the chosen variant, not the authoritative palette or default primary label.</p><div class="docs-grid">{['cb-ui','hui'].map(system=><div class="dmf-ui docs-entry" data-system={system} data-color-mode="light" data-contrast-alternative><h3>{system==='cb-ui'?'CB':'HUI'} outline alternative</h3><Button as="a" href="/components/button/" variant="outline">Review Button variants</Button></div>)}</div><p>Interactive components consuming primary/primary-foreground inherit the same policy; filled Button, loading actions and Block submissions are representative affected states. Disabled opacity and overlays must be evaluated separately. Keyboard focus, non-text cues and unrelated contrast findings remain required checks.</p></section>
